    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d381">

                <pb facs="0583" n="495" sameAs="frus:frus1892/pg495"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Grubb to Mr. Blaine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1892-05-25"><hi rendition="#italic">May 25, 1892</hi></date>.
                        (Received June 13.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 257.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I had the honor to send you last night the
                    following telegram: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Royal decree published to-day removing restrictions of decree of November
                            9, 1887, on pork coming from the United States. All that is now required
                            is certificate of origin and of inspection in accordance with the law of
                            the United States March 3, 1891. All greases prepared by action of fire
                            and also fat bacon are exempt from inspection here and from bringing a
                            certificate of inspection from whence they come.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>I now inclose a note from the Duke of Tetuan and translation dated May 24, 1892,
                    formally announcing the removal of the restriction upon the importation of
                    American pork into this country and the adjacent Spanish islands.</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">E. Burd Grubb.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d381-a1.xml" xpointer="d381-a1"/>
            </div>
